      "text": "To solve the problem, we will first set up the equations for the given conditions. Let the four integers be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). According to the problem:\n\n\\[a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when the sum of these four integers is divided by 11. Therefore, we calculate:\n\n\\[a + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\nLet's compute the sum of \\(2 + 4 + 6 + 8\\):\n\n\\[2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11:\n\n\\[20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ R } 9\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when 20 is divided by 11 is 9. This means that the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{9}\\]\n\nTo confirm this, we can use Python to verify the calculations.\n```python\n# Given remainders\nremainders = [2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n# Sum of the remainders\nsum_of_remainders = sum(remainders)\n\n# Finding the remainder of the sum when divided by 11\nremainder = sum_of_remainders % 11\nprint(remainder)\n```",
